{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1283 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "22b8e5d34a3b467ea8461d66dc293404ad000b2d2ed17ec4e79fc84961813bd5" :edb/db-before-t 1282 :edb/db-after-t 1283 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534595 50 #inst "2026-10-08T01:56:48.738Z" 13194139534595 true] [17592186128808 1100 "Which of the following sets is equivalent to $S = \\{2, 4, 8, 2, 4, 2\\}$?\n\n1. $\\{\\{2\\},4,8\\}$\n2. $\\{2,4,8\\}$\n3. $\\{2,8\\}$" 13194139534595 false] [17592186128808 1100 "Which of the following sets is equivalent to $S = \\{2, 4, 8, 2, 4, 2\\}?$ \n\n- $\\{\\{2\\},4,8\\}$\n\n- $\\{2,4,8\\}$\n\n- $\\{2,8\\}$" 13194139534595 true] [17592186128808 1145 "Two sets are equivalent if they contain the same elements. It doesn't matter if the elements are listed differently or if one set has duplicates and the other does not.\n\nTo determine which of the given sets is equivalent to $S$, we start by listing the elements of $S$, ignoring any duplicates:\n$2, \\qquad 4, \\qquad 8$\n\nTherefore, the only set equivalent to $S$ is $\\{2,4,8\\}$ since it contains the same elements as $S$.\n\nThe other sets are not equivalent to $S{:}$\n\n- $\\{\\{2\\},4,8\\}$ has the element $\\{2\\}$ that is not in $S$. Note that $\\{2\\}\\neq 2$.\n- $\\{2,8\\}$ is missing the element $4$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534595 false] [17592186128808 1145 "Two sets are equivalent if they contain the same elements. It doesn't matter if the elements are listed differently or if one set has duplicates and the other does not.\n\nTo determine which of the given sets is equivalent to $S,$ we start by listing the elements of $S,$ ignoring any duplicates:\n\n$$\n2, \\qquad 4, \\qquad 8\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only set equivalent to $S$ is $\\{2,4,8\\}$ since it contains the same elements as $S.$\n\nThe other sets are not equivalent to $S{:}$\n\n- $\\{\\{2\\},4,8\\}$ has the element $\\{2\\}$ that is not in $S.$  Note that $\\{2\\}\\neq 2$.\n\n- $\\{2,8\\}$ is missing the element $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534595 true] [17592186128809 1100 "Which of the following sets are equivalent to $A = \\{0, 1, 2, 3, \\ldots\\} ?$\n\n- $\\mathbb{N}$\n\n- $\\mathbb{N}_{0}$\n\n- $\\mathbb{Z}$\n\n- $\\mathbb{Z}^{+}$" 13194139534595 true] [17592186128809 1100 "Which of the following sets are equivalent to $A = \\{0, 1, 2, 3, \\ldots\\}$?\n\n1. $\\mathbb{N}$\n2. $\\mathbb{N}_{0}$\n3. $\\mathbb{Z}$\n4. $\\mathbb{Z}^{+}$" 13194139534595 false] [17592186128809 1145 "The set $A$ is the set of positive integers and zero. It is denoted by $\\mathbb{N}_{0}$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\mathbb{N}_{0}$.\n\nThe other options are *not* equivalent to $A{:}$\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}$ does not include the element zero, and $0\\in A$.\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}$ includes the elements $-1,-2,-3,\\ldots$, and $-1 \\not \\in A, -2\\notin A, -3\\notin A, \\ldots\\,$.\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}^{+}$ does not include the element zero, and $0\\in A$." 13194139534595 false] [17592186128809 1145 "The set $A$ is the set of positive integers and zero. It is denoted by $\\mathbb{N}_{0}$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\mathbb{N}_{0}.$\n\nThe other options are *not* equivalent to $A{:}$\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}$ does not include the element zero, and $0\\in A.$\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}$ includes the elements $-1,-2,-3,\\ldots,$ and $-1 \\not \\in A, -2\\notin A, -3\\notin A, \\ldots\\,.$\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}^{+}$ does not include the element zero, and $0\\in A.$" 13194139534595 true] [17592186128810 1100 "Which of the following sets are equivalent to $S = \\{ a, \\{ b \\}, c, \\{ b \\}, a \\}?$\n\n- $\\{ a, \\{b\\}, c \\}$\n\n- $\\{ a, c, b, \\{b\\} \\}$\n\n- $\\{ a, \\{b\\}, c, d \\}$" 13194139534595 true] [17592186128810 1100 "Which of the following sets are equivalent to $S = \\{a, \\{b \\}, c, \\{b \\}, a \\}$?\n\n1. $\\{a, \\{b\\}, c \\}$\n2. $\\{a, c, b, \\{b\\} \\}$\n3. $\\{a, \\{b\\}, c, d \\}$" 13194139534595 false] [17592186128810 1145 "Two sets are equivalent if they contain the same elements. It doesn't matter if the elements are listed differently or if one set has duplicates and the other does not.\n\nTo determine which of the given sets is equivalent to $S$, we start by listing the elements of $S$, ignoring any duplicates:\n\n$$\na, \\qquad \\{b\\}, \\qquad c\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only set equivalent to $S$ is $\\{a, \\{b\\}, c \\}$ since it contains the same elements as $S$.\n\nThe other sets are not equivalent to $S{:}$\n\n- Set II *not* equivalent to $S$. It has an element $b$ that is not in $S$. Note that $\\{b\\} \\neq b$.\n- Set III is *not* equivalent to $S$. It has an element $d$ that is not in $S$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139534595 false] [17592186128810 1145 "Two sets are equivalent if they contain the same elements. It doesn't matter if the elements are listed differently or if one set has duplicates and the other does not.\n\nTo determine which of the given sets is equivalent to $S,$ we start by listing the elements of $S,$ ignoring any duplicates:\n\n$$\na, \\qquad \\{b\\}, \\qquad c\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only set equivalent to $S$ is $\\{ a, \\{b\\}, c \\}$ since it contains the same elements as $S.$\n\nThe other sets are not equivalent to $S{:}$\n\n- Set II *not* equivalent to $S.$ It has an element $b$ that is not in $S.$ Note that $\\{b\\} \\neq b.$\n\n- Set III is *not* equivalent to $S.$ It has an element $d$ that is not in $S.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139534595 true] [17592186129253 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297746 13194139534595 true] [17592186129253 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297753 13194139534595 true] [17592186129253 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297760 13194139534595 true] [17592186129253 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297767 13194139534595 true] [17592186129253 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297774 13194139534595 true] [17592186129254 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297732 13194139534595 true] [17592186129254 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297739 13194139534595 true] [17592186129254 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297781 13194139534595 true] [17592186129254 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297788 13194139534595 true] [17592186129254 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297795 13194139534595 true] [17592186129255 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297802 13194139534595 true] [17592186129255 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297809 13194139534595 true] [17592186129255 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297816 13194139534595 true] [17592186129255 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297823 13194139534595 true] [17592186129495 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534595 true] [17592186129495 1100 "Which of the following intervals is equivalent to $R_{0}^{+}$?" 13194139534595 false] [17592186129495 1100 "Which of the following intervals is equivalent to ${R}_{0}^{+}?$" 13194139534595 true] [17592186129495 1145 "The set ${R}_{0}^{+}$ denotes the set of positive real numbers or zero. It is equivalent to the following interval:\n\n$$\n[0,\\infty )\n$$\n\nThe other options are *not* equivalent to ${R}_{0}^{+}:$\n\n- The interval $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$ includes the negative real numbers.\n\n- The interval $(0,\\infty )$ does not include the zero.\n\n- The interval $(-\\infty ,0)$ does not include the positive real numbers or zero.\n\n- The interval $(-\\infty ,0]$ does not include the positive real numbers." 13194139534595 true] [17592186297732 1017 #edb/ref 17592186297733 13194139534595 true] [17592186297732 1089 "q-180821" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297732 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534595 true] [17592186297732 1100 "Which set is equivalent to $S={0,{1},{0},1,0,{0}}?$" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297732 1113 #uuid "26d0ae9a-cd8a-5695-b354-4253c50dee18" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297732 1145 "Two sets are equivalent if they contain the same elements. It doesn't matter if the elements are listed differently or if one set has duplicates and the other does not.\n\nTo determine which of the given sets is equivalent to $S,$ we start by listing the elements of $S,$ ignoring any duplicates:\n\n$$\n0,\\,{1},\\,{0},\\,1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only set equivalent to $S$ is ${0,1,{0},{1}}$ since it contains the same elements as $S.$\n\nThe other sets are not equivalent to $S:$\n\n- ${0,1,{1}}$ is missing the element ${0}$ (note that ${0}\\ne 0$).\n\n- ${{0},0,1}$ is missing the element ${1}$ (note that ${1}\\ne 1$).\n\n- ${0,1,{0,1},{0},{1}}$ has the element ${0,1}$ that is not in $S.$\n\n- ${0,1,{1},2,{0}}$ has the element $2$ that is not in $S.$" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297733 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297734 13194139534595 true] [17592186297733 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297735 13194139534595 true] [17592186297733 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297736 13194139534595 true] [17592186297733 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297737 13194139534595 true] [17592186297733 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297738 13194139534595 true] [17592186297733 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534595 true] [17592186297733 1041 "selection" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297733 1104 #edb/ref 17592186297736 13194139534595 true] [17592186297733 1110 #uuid "078835d0-f253-5599-8106-01cebf808753" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297734 1034 "{0,1,{1},2,{0}}" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534595 true] [17592186297734 1111 #uuid "e5077221-34db-5974-b966-4fe82a633df1" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297735 1034 "{0,1,{0,1},{0},{1}}" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534595 true] [17592186297735 1111 #uuid "19845da1-3a20-500e-a250-ee19d92a74ce" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297736 1034 "{0,1,{0},{1}}" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297736 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534595 true] [17592186297736 1111 #uuid "b022c4e6-1d12-59f3-99d3-3bfe4921b1c9" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297737 1034 "{{0},0,1}" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297737 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534595 true] [17592186297737 1111 #uuid "fd10b6dd-275a-5eca-b95a-771de1143e34" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297738 1034 "{0,1,{1}}" 13194139534595 true] [17592186297738 1103 #